+ * Return where the mapping for the dirty blocks [@offset, @offset + @len) of
+ * @folio can end, at most @end: at the end of the run holding @offset, so the
+ * scan for dirty folios need not go further either.  With clusters smaller
+ * than a folio, the clean blocks of a dirty folio, and the leading ones of
+ * the dirty folios that follow, can be delalloc clusters that the buffered
+ * write in progress has not copied into yet: stop where they start, but
+ * always cover the blocks iomap passed in.  Larger clusters are zeroed or
+ * copied whole before writeback can see them dirty.
